====== Leetcode 69. Sqrt(x) =======

Step-by-step algorithm to find the square root of a number using Binary Search:

Step 1: Initialize two variables:

l = 0

h = x

Step 2: Repeat the following steps while l is less than or equal to h.

Step 3: Calculate the middle value:

mid = l + (h - l) / 2

Step 4: Compute mid × mid (use long type to avoid overflow).

Step 5: Compare mid × mid with x.

Sub-step 5a: If mid × mid is greater than x,
move to the left half by setting
h = mid - 1

Sub-step 5b: If mid × mid is less than x,
move to the right half by setting
l = mid + 1

Sub-step 5c: If mid × mid is equal to x,
return mid (exact square root found).

Step 6: Continue this process until l becomes greater than h.

Step 7: When the loop ends, return h.

h will store the integer part of the square root (floor value).

Time Complexity:
Binary search reduces the search space by half each time.
Time Complexity = O(log x)

Space Complexity:
Only a few variables are used.
Space Complexity = O(1)


          ----------------> Code <-------------------

class Solution {
    public int mySqrt(int x) {
        int l=0, h=x;

        while(l<=h){
            int mid=l+(h-l)/2;
            if((long)mid*mid>x){
                h=mid-1;
            }else if((long)mid*mid<x){
                l=mid+1;
            }else{
                return Math.round(mid);
            }
        }
        return h;
    }
}
